@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-120b-indexation`
IMPORT `ito-il26-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Figures PUBLISHED BY THE ISRAEL TAX AUTHORITY. NOT ENCODED LAW.
--
-- The Regulations print no amount: Schedule A takes the tax from ss 121 and 121B "as adjusted under s 120B" and the
-- credit point from the Ordinance. The two amounts that Schedule A needs for a tax year are therefore inputs of
-- the rules, and this module records what the Authority has published, with the provenance that the rows IL-01
-- and IL-03 recorded. It re-fetches nothing: the sources below are RECORDED BY POINTER AND HASH in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/SOURCES.json, not deposited, and the figures are carried from the
-- IL-01 and IL-03 modules' own quotations of them, not re-read from the PDFs by this row.
--
--   [itc135-2025] explanatory notes to form 135 for 2025, sha256 207412d97ed3daa65f49d42ae7e68e62e67e1f0dba674be40962989f7c9ad0eb,
--                 p. 4, section ח: the credit point for tax year 2025 is NIS 2,904 (as IL-01 quotes it, ito-credit-points-published-figures.l4).
--   [booklet-2026] the monthly withholding booklet (cover title: auxiliary table for computing income tax on salary and wages), sha256 282bb886ccae1cc718840127af378fce88ca37ee3b2b9f00ed2cd44467e86285:
--                 p. 9, the credit point is NIS 242 a month (as IL-01 records it);
--                 p. 8, the s 121B(a) amount is NIS 721,560 a year, NIS 60,130 a month (as IL-03 quotes it,
--                 ito-il03-published-figures.l4).
--
-- Carrying these to tax years 2026 and 2027 is not done here by copying: s 120B(e)(1) (row IL-03's mechanism,
-- vendored beside this file) fixes each adjusted amount in 2025, 2026 and 2027 at its 1 January 2024 figure after
-- rounding, so the rules below pass the Authority's figure through IL-03's `s 120B — the amount in force in the
-- tax year` and let it say so.
--
-- What is NOT here: the Authority's monthly TABLE (the booklet's schedule of tax by salary) of Schedule A item (6).
-- It is not deposited; ito-il26-regulations.l4 declines to answer "what the table says".
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Figures published by the Israel Tax Authority — not encoded law`

-- Dummy index readings: s 120B(e)(1) makes the answer for 2025 to 2027 independent of the index.
@ref ITO s 120B(e)(1) (row IL-03)
GIVETH AN `Index readings for a period`
`index readings that a frozen year does not read` MEANS
    `Index readings for a period` WITH
        `index last published before the start of the period` IS 100
        `index last published before the end of the period`   IS 100

@ref ITO s 120B(e)(1) (row IL-03); [itc135-2025] p. 4 for the 2,904
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of amount adjusted under section 120B`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`the frozen-year facts for` k `in` `the tax year` `from` `the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding` MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS k
        `tax year`                                                      IS `the tax year`
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS `the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding`
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `index readings that a frozen year does not read`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS NOTHING
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS `the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding`

-- The two amounts Schedule A needs, for the tax years 2026 and 2027 (the years IL-03 prints section 121 for).
@ref [itc135-2025] p. 4; [booklet-2026] p. 8; ITO s 120B(e)(1)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `The annual figures for the tax year`
`the annual figures published for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    IF   `the tax year` AT LEAST 2026 AND `the tax year` AT MOST 2027
    THEN `The annual figures for the tax year` WITH
            `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` IS `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the frozen-year facts for` `an income ceiling` `in` `the tax year` `from` 721_560)
            `the value of one credit point`                           IS `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the frozen-year facts for` `the amount of a credit point` `in` `the tax year` `from` 2_904)
    ELSE `no annual figures published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year have been sourced in this encoding`

@ref Israel Tax Authority; no figures for this tax year sourced in row IL-26
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no annual figures published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year have been sourced in this encoding` MEANS
    REFUSE "no annual figures published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year have been sourced in this encoding"
